  "homepage": "https://davelab10.github.io/portofolio/",
  "tests_url": "https://github.com/davelab10/railcall-stripe-invoicing/blob/main/TESTING.md",
  "description": "Governed Stripe accounts receivable. Twenty-five commands under stripe.billing.*, built for the solo consultant or small agency that runs billing from an assistant and does not want a model deciding on its own to email a five-figure invoice. Twelve read freely, thirteen stop at the airlock for approval.\n\nBILLING\nbill_client {\"email\":\"ada@acme.com\",\"description\":\"July retainer\",\"amount_cents\":250000} is composite: find-or-create, draft, finalize, send, four Stripe calls behind one approval.\ninvoice_create {\"customer_id\":\"cus_X\",\"line_items\":[{\"description\":\"Design\",\"amount_cents\":96000}]} is composite too: opens the invoice, then attaches each line item. Nothing is emailed.\ninvoice_send {\"invoice_id\":\"in_X\"} finalizes and delivers, refusing paid or void invoices.\ninvoice_void {\"invoice_id\":\"in_X\"} voids an open invoice.\ninvoice_get {\"invoice_id\":\"in_X\"} and invoice_list {\"status\":\"open\"} read one or many, with outstanding totals rolled up.\n\nCOLLECTIONS\naging_report {} buckets every open invoice 0-30, 31-60, 61-90 and 90+ days overdue.\ncredit_note_create {\"invoice_id\":\"in_X\",\"amount_cents\":5000} reduces an open invoice, a paid one routes to refund_create.\nrefund_create {\"charge_id\":\"ch_X\"} refunds in the same structured shape as every other command.\n\nCUSTOMERS\ncustomer_summary {\"customer_id\":\"cus_X\"} rolls up profile, invoices, subscriptions and lifetime paid in one call.\ncustomer_find {\"email\":\"ada@acme.com\"} and customer_create {\"email\":\"ada@acme.com\",\"name\":\"Ada\"} do the obvious things.\npayment_method_list {\"customer_id\":\"cus_X\"} lists cards by brand and last four, never full numbers.\n\nSUBSCRIPTIONS\nsubscription_list {\"customer_id\":\"cus_X\"} and subscription_cancel {\"subscription_id\":\"sub_X\",\"at_period_end\":true}, defaulting to period end.\n\nINCENTIVES\ncoupon_create {\"percent_off\":15,\"duration\":\"once\"}, coupon_list {}, and promotion_code_create {\"coupon_id\":\"acALYzHV\",\"code\":\"PAYNOW15\"}.\n\nCATALOG AND USAGE\nproduct_create {\"name\":\"API access\"} and product_list {} define what you sell. price_create {\"product_id\":\"prod_X\",\"unit_amount_cents\":1500} defaults to one-time; add interval for recurring, or meter_id plus interval for usage-based via Billing Meters. price_list {} reads prices back. usage_record_create {\"meter_id\":\"mtr_X\",\"customer_id\":\"cus_X\",\"value\":42} logs consumption. usage_summary_list {\"meter_id\":\"mtr_X\",\"customer_id\":\"cus_X\"} reads it back after roughly 30 seconds of aggregation.\n\nAUTHORIZATION\nmandate_get {\"mandate_id\":\"mandate_X\"} retrieves a standing authorization for future debits, never created directly, only a side effect of a SEPA or ACH setup flow.\n\nTRUST\nEvery money-moving call carries a Stripe Idempotency-Key derived from the airlock payload hash: one approval is at most one write. A missing helper is a hard error, never a silent fallback.\n\nTROUBLESHOOTING\nA 401 means the key is revoked, mistyped, or from another account: re-save it under Integrations. Nothing working with a valid-looking key usually means sk_test_ paired against live-mode ids, or the reverse.\n\nSETUP\nOne Stripe secret key in the local vault under STRIPE_SECRET_KEY, never in a request body, payload hash, or receipt. sk_test_ keys work end to end.\n\ncontest:2026Q3",
